{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization of the companion paper's refutation of McNamara and Steingrimsson's Question 9.5 (2015) via an explicit 19-element closed interval [213, 2574613] of largest rank size 7 and width 8, and of its proof that for every k >= 1 there exists a principal downset [empty, tau_k] whose width exceeds its largest rank size by exactly k. Companion write-up and dated prior-work searches (arXiv, CORE 2026-11-20, Google Scholar 2026-11-22, Zenodo, DataCite, HAL, OSF, and Elizalde-McNamara 2015 / Vatter 2026) are published at https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/pattern-poset-not-sperner; no prior non-Sperner interval of the classical pattern poset was found in those logged searches, while Pouzet-Rosenberg (1986), Burosch et al. (1990, 1996), and print monographs remain unread/unsearched. Coverage by this package's Palomar comparison: of the companion paper's 9 main results, 2 are compared in Lean in full (22%; Corollary 1 and Theorem 3) and 2 in part (Proposition 2: the interval's size 19 and largest rank size 7, not its full list of rank sizes; Theorem 8: deficiency exactly k for some principal downset, not for the named downset [empty, tau_k]); Theorem 4 and Propositions 5, 6 and 7, with the full Proposition 2 and Theorem 8, are proved in this package's Lean library but not compared; Proposition 9 is by certificate only; Conjecture 10 is open and not counted.",
